 adds no managed activation, write/recovery handoff or retirement authority.
+
+## Independent writer and reader deadlines
+
+The opt-in deadline profile uses the held canonical actor binding and matching
+manifest entry to bind one finite per-actor write or reader window separately
+from the role's exact finite `VALID UNTIL`. Dedicated reader ACLs admit only
+the getter in this profile. Writer submit and replay, writer getter, dependent
+recorder authorization for Resume, provisional return and literal COMMIT
+check database time. The independent reader's public getter authenticates
+the scoped caller before consulting a target. It then checks the existing
+target-dependent catalog and original rules. All getter relation checks
+retain one STABLE parent snapshot. The final reader check samples only the
+scalar database clock, after materializing the canonical response. These
+are recognized checks within one supported standalone getter statement.
+Response delivery can lag them.
+
+The focused direct fixture keeps the accepted 35/180-second role logins,
+assigns recorder writes to 24 seconds and independent readback to 42 seconds
+from the same issuance instant, and holds the existing transaction and
+statement limits. It checks a writer staged before cutoff, refused literal
+COMMIT while still able to log in, exact independent readback, eventual
+fresh writer login denial, and application read refusal while the reader
+still authenticates. An independent table lock holds one absent getter
+after scoped authorization until the final-return check crosses the read
+cutoff. There is no production TTL selection, handoff or owner-separated
+terminal retirement composition in this source.
